1
00:00:18,418 --> 00:00:21,888
Do you think Florence is the kind of person

2
00:00:21,888 --> 00:00:25,458
who will just let others step on her?

3
00:00:25,458 --> 00:00:28,228
Do you think that Florence
is the type of person

4
00:00:28,228 --> 00:00:30,503
who will not fight back
if someone is trying to oppress her?

5
00:00:30,503 --> 00:00:34,006
If there's one person who can fight back,
that's Florence.

6
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:51,392
That's bad.

7
00:00:52,285 --> 00:00:55,087
How is the view from the floor?

8
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:15,581
Hey!

9
00:01:15,581 --> 00:01:17,592
You already saw that I fell

10
00:01:17,592 --> 00:01:19,964
and now you're asking me
to hold on to your drink?

11
00:01:19,964 --> 00:01:24,250
We were minding our own business
and then she suddenly meddles.

12
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:26,586
She's not aware of her place here.

13
00:01:26,586 --> 00:01:29,056
She labeled us as if we were
the villains in her life.

14
00:01:29,056 --> 00:01:32,759
Well, if that's what she believes,
then I guess we should play the part.

15
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:36,129
I heard a rumor that
there's this secret sorority

16
00:01:36,129 --> 00:01:38,762
of popular girls on campus.

17
00:01:38,762 --> 00:01:42,068
They are known by the name Aylip.

18
00:01:42,068 --> 00:01:43,169
Aylip?

19
00:01:43,169 --> 00:01:44,938
They're a very powerful group.

20
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:47,674
And, based on my sources,

21
00:01:47,674 --> 00:01:51,611
there's someone new
that they're declaring persona-non-grata

22
00:01:51,611 --> 00:01:54,305
on the first day of school.

23
00:01:54,305 --> 00:01:57,283
I saw a girl who looks exactly
like you the other day.

24
00:01:57,283 --> 00:02:01,754
I don't believe in what they say
"leap of blood" but...

25
00:02:02,387 --> 00:02:03,955
I felt something.

26
00:02:03,955 --> 00:02:05,590
Is she my grandchild?

27
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:07,492
Is Celestina alive?

28
00:02:07,492 --> 00:02:08,741
I'll just use the CR.

29
00:02:08,741 --> 00:02:10,562
This is off-limits.

30
00:02:10,562 --> 00:02:11,850
Why?

31
00:02:11,850 --> 00:02:15,566
I said this is off-limits.

32
00:02:17,402 --> 00:02:18,703
Did you do that on purpose?

33
00:02:18,703 --> 00:02:22,641
If you don't want to be hit,
find a different place,

34
00:02:22,641 --> 00:02:25,509
not here where we are playing.

35
00:03:22,591 --> 00:03:24,577
Don't! Who are you?

36
00:03:24,577 --> 00:03:27,274
Let go of me! What's with you?

37
00:03:27,274 --> 00:03:29,168
Do you often hang out here?

38
00:03:29,168 --> 00:03:31,570
I like their iced tea.

39
00:03:32,377 --> 00:03:33,578
Troy.

40
00:03:33,578 --> 00:03:35,247
Wait, Babe.

41
00:03:35,247 --> 00:03:37,215
Do I know you?

42
00:03:37,215 --> 00:03:40,028
Have you seen Florence?

43
00:03:40,028 --> 00:03:41,986
Florence is missing?

44
00:03:43,294 --> 00:03:45,390
Who are you? What do you need from me?

45
00:03:45,390 --> 00:03:47,492
Let me go, please.

46
00:03:47,492 --> 00:03:50,895
What's with you? Who are you?

47
00:03:52,654 --> 00:03:54,215
Tristan?

48
00:03:55,185 --> 00:03:56,768
Aldus?

49
00:03:56,768 --> 00:04:00,105
What are you doing? You fools!

50
00:04:00,105 --> 00:04:01,873
We have no choice.

51
00:04:01,873 --> 00:04:04,242
You are in big trouble, Florence.

52
00:04:04,242 --> 00:04:06,077
Me, trouble?

53
00:04:06,077 --> 00:04:07,912
Why?

54
00:04:12,250 --> 00:04:13,485
That's my picture.

55
00:04:13,485 --> 00:04:15,353
How did they get that?

56
00:04:15,353 --> 00:04:18,957
TWPS? What's written there?
The West Philippine Sea?

57
00:04:18,957 --> 00:04:22,027
No, The Worst Person in School.

58
00:04:22,027 --> 00:04:25,966
It means, you have offended
an influential girl in school.

59
00:04:25,966 --> 00:04:30,343
That's why now,
you're the target enemy of everyone.

60
00:04:30,343 --> 00:04:32,470
What did you do?

61
00:04:35,876 --> 00:04:39,430
The most important question now is,

62
00:04:39,430 --> 00:04:42,299
why are you sweet to me all of a sudden?

63
00:04:46,550 --> 00:04:48,986
I'm touched by your concern for me.

64
00:04:48,986 --> 00:04:52,389
I knew it, you two are kind-hearted too.

65
00:04:52,389 --> 00:04:54,625
Didn't you hear what we told you?

66
00:04:54,625 --> 00:04:57,361
You're the target enemy #1 of Aylip

67
00:04:57,361 --> 00:04:59,029
and they have a lot of members
here in the school.

68
00:04:59,029 --> 00:05:02,232
So you have a big problem.

69
00:05:02,232 --> 00:05:03,618
I heard what you said.

70
00:05:03,618 --> 00:05:05,936
Do you think I'm not scared?

71
00:05:05,936 --> 00:05:08,671
But what can I do? Hide in a hole?

72
00:05:08,671 --> 00:05:11,308
What do you want me to do, drop out from GU?

73
00:05:11,308 --> 00:05:13,633
Mope in one corner,

74
00:05:13,633 --> 00:05:16,980
forget all my dreams because
those Aylips don't like me?

75
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:20,249
They're mad at me and
now I'm target #1 enemy?

76
00:05:24,288 --> 00:05:26,039
It's like this.

77
00:05:26,039 --> 00:05:31,361
I saw a student they were bullying earlier
and I meddled.

78
00:05:31,361 --> 00:05:34,697
Maybe that's why they're picking on me.

79
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:38,616
Do you know my father's favorite saying?

80
00:05:40,837 --> 00:05:45,809
The way to the heart of a man or woman
is through their stomach.

81
00:05:45,809 --> 00:05:48,145
What?

82
00:05:48,145 --> 00:05:51,748
- She's kidding.
- What are you talking about?

83
00:05:51,748 --> 00:05:54,851
But I don't think that applies to you guys

84
00:05:54,851 --> 00:05:58,021
because it seems like your tummy
and intestines are not good.

85
00:05:58,021 --> 00:06:01,692
It looks like there's a blockage
going to your heart as well.

86
00:06:01,692 --> 00:06:04,461
So what's more applicable to you is

87
00:06:04,461 --> 00:06:06,863
"the only thing necessary
for the triumph of evil

88
00:06:06,863 --> 00:06:09,072
is for good men to do nothing."

89
00:06:09,072 --> 00:06:12,336
And with cases like this
that you're bullying someone

90
00:06:12,336 --> 00:06:17,807
and there's a witness like me
when we won't do anything and be quiet...

91
00:06:22,746 --> 00:06:28,418
Wait, did you kidnap me just to tell me this?

92
00:06:28,418 --> 00:06:31,054
You could've texted me.

93
00:06:31,054 --> 00:06:33,490
This is more fun.

94
00:06:33,490 --> 00:06:35,659
Be thankful it's just this.

95
00:06:35,659 --> 00:06:37,327
- Is that so?
- You should've seen your face.

96
00:06:37,327 --> 00:06:38,795
You fools!

97
00:06:38,795 --> 00:06:39,796
- You're really...
- Just a little push

98
00:06:39,796 --> 00:06:41,349
and you were about to cry.

99
00:06:42,232 --> 00:06:45,235
But seriously, what's your plan?

100
00:06:45,235 --> 00:06:46,940
Your life here won't be easy,

101
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,771
especially since you've offended
one of the influential groups

102
00:06:48,771 --> 00:06:51,240
here in school.

103
00:06:52,014 --> 00:06:54,956
Well, I will do what I can do,

104
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:57,884
and that is to fight
and not give up the fight.

105
00:06:57,884 --> 00:07:00,780
I was able to survive the Ferells,
what more of them?

106
00:07:00,780 --> 00:07:01,818
Well then, good luck.

107
00:07:01,818 --> 00:07:04,387
Yes, you need a lot of luck.

108
00:07:08,611 --> 00:07:10,769
Hey, where are you going?

109
00:07:10,769 --> 00:07:13,171
Can't you take this off?

110
00:07:14,998 --> 00:07:17,167
Fun, fun. What's so funny?

111
00:07:17,167 --> 00:07:20,303
Spotlight. You're an expert in kidnapping.

112
00:07:23,106 --> 00:07:25,308
Let's go our separate ways, Florence.

113
00:07:26,143 --> 00:07:27,911
Don't come too close.

114
00:07:27,911 --> 00:07:30,814
You're on your own
and we've warned you already.

115
00:07:30,814 --> 00:07:33,917
I thought you were really concerned about me.

116
00:07:33,917 --> 00:07:35,986
The Aylip is powerful
and the girls might stay away from us

117
00:07:35,986 --> 00:07:37,757
once they find out that we know you.

118
00:07:37,757 --> 00:07:41,725
I agree. And if you need help, don't call us.

119
00:07:41,725 --> 00:07:43,760
Call Owen and Troy.

120
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:44,995
Or Nero.

121
00:07:44,995 --> 00:07:46,674
Bye. Let's go.

122
00:08:14,057 --> 00:08:19,362
I don't think they'll come here.

123
00:08:21,031 --> 00:08:23,100
Hopefully, they won't be here.

124
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:25,401
There's no one here.

125
00:08:33,176 --> 00:08:34,760
Nero?

126
00:08:38,115 --> 00:08:42,885
So, this is the perfect meeting place
for both of us?

127
00:09:17,521 --> 00:09:20,557
I knew it, I'd find you here.

128
00:09:20,557 --> 00:09:22,792
Did you receive my messages?

129
00:09:25,555 --> 00:09:27,664
Message?

130
00:09:27,664 --> 00:09:29,900
What message?

131
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:32,468
I didn't get any message from you.

132
00:09:33,437 --> 00:09:38,619
No texts or calls, not even an email.

133
00:09:38,619 --> 00:09:43,045
You used to send me cute little messages
using messenger birds.

134
00:09:45,877 --> 00:09:49,012
<i>So those messages weren't for me?</i>

135
00:09:52,055 --> 00:09:54,257
But even that...

136
00:09:54,257 --> 00:09:56,993
I haven't received anything from you.

137
00:10:04,404 --> 00:10:07,741
You haven't spoken to me since last year.

138
00:10:07,741 --> 00:10:10,940
It's like you just suddenly disappeared.

139
00:10:17,690 --> 00:10:19,817
I'm sorry.

140
00:10:19,817 --> 00:10:24,688
Just stop pretending like
you've been sending me messages,

141
00:10:24,688 --> 00:10:26,857
because the truth is...

142
00:10:26,857 --> 00:10:28,991
you just suddenly disappeared.

143
00:10:30,961 --> 00:10:35,565
Nero, I just want to talk to you...

144
00:10:35,565 --> 00:10:38,067
to settle things once and for all.

145
00:10:38,735 --> 00:10:44,473
I can't keep doing this,
just figuring things out by myself.

146
00:10:46,204 --> 00:10:48,852
It's just better if we move on.

147
00:10:49,582 --> 00:10:54,883
Sometimes I feel like you're no longer
the Nero that I've known before.

148
00:10:54,883 --> 00:10:57,621
And if we stay in this relationship,

149
00:10:57,621 --> 00:11:04,493
the more I'd get hurt
and the more we'll hurt each other.

150
00:11:10,219 --> 00:11:11,968
I agree.

151
00:11:11,968 --> 00:11:13,937
You're right.

152
00:11:13,937 --> 00:11:16,672
It'll be better for both of us.

153
00:11:43,592 --> 00:11:45,902
Why did you assume too much, Florence?

154
00:11:45,902 --> 00:11:48,772
Do you really believe that Nero
will send you...

155
00:11:48,772 --> 00:11:50,307
Florence.

156
00:11:50,307 --> 00:11:52,909
I've been looking for you
for quite a while now.

157
00:11:52,909 --> 00:11:54,744
Are you okay?

158
00:11:58,915 --> 00:12:00,883
Why do you look that way?

159
00:12:01,573 --> 00:12:03,541
Did someone hurt you?

160
00:12:07,390 --> 00:12:09,355
Have you heard about Aylip?

161
00:12:10,180 --> 00:12:13,015
Tristan and Aldus talked to me already.

162
00:12:13,930 --> 00:12:15,999
You have to be careful, Florence.

163
00:12:15,999 --> 00:12:19,668
We don't know what's going on in their minds.

164
00:12:20,770 --> 00:12:24,039
You know it'll be better
if you ride with us going home.

165
00:12:24,741 --> 00:12:27,477
I can even accompany you here in school.

166
00:12:27,477 --> 00:12:30,614
Owen, I promise,
you don't have to worry about me.

167
00:12:30,614 --> 00:12:32,983
I want to be alone first.

168
00:12:32,983 --> 00:12:35,451
I can handle myself.

169
00:12:49,299 --> 00:12:51,200
Florence!

170
00:12:52,402 --> 00:12:54,817
Hey, wait! What's with you?

171
00:12:58,141 --> 00:12:59,245
Yes, Troy?

172
00:12:59,245 --> 00:13:02,422
If you're here to tell me that
the group Aylip has declared me as TWPS,

173
00:13:02,422 --> 00:13:05,638
I know that already.
And I already know that all people here

174
00:13:05,638 --> 00:13:07,317
are watching my every move,
that's all of them.

175
00:13:07,317 --> 00:13:10,086
But thank you for your concern
but I'm not scared.

176
00:13:10,086 --> 00:13:11,955
And for your information,
I'm not intimidated,

177
00:13:11,955 --> 00:13:14,324
and the more I'm not terrified of them.

178
00:13:14,324 --> 00:13:15,692
But you know, I've realized,

179
00:13:15,692 --> 00:13:19,128
they're starting to make trouble.
Well then, I'll end it.

180
00:13:23,733 --> 00:13:26,175
What did she say?

181
00:13:26,175 --> 00:13:29,244
I even ran, and that's tiring.

182
00:13:43,286 --> 00:13:46,233
You, you, you, you, and all of you.

183
00:13:46,233 --> 00:13:50,444
Are you the reason why the sorority, Aylip,
is picking on me?

184
00:13:50,444 --> 00:13:52,429
What's your problem?

185
00:13:52,429 --> 00:13:55,298
Is there nothing you can do with your lives?
Are you bored?

186
00:13:55,298 --> 00:13:57,567
Do you think I'm scared of you?

187
00:13:57,567 --> 00:14:02,405
And you...
Will you really let them step on you?

188
00:14:02,405 --> 00:14:05,275
What's with you? Have you gone crazy?

189
00:14:05,275 --> 00:14:08,435
And for both of you,

190
00:14:08,435 --> 00:14:12,185
what satisfaction are you getting
from stepping on someone else?

191
00:14:12,185 --> 00:14:15,752
Because I came here to learn,
to make myself whole,

192
00:14:15,752 --> 00:14:18,085
and achieve my dreams for my family.

193
00:14:18,085 --> 00:14:22,559
How about you?
I think you came here to belittle others.

194
00:14:22,559 --> 00:14:24,260
What kind of person are you?

195
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:27,897
How did your parents raise you?

196
00:14:31,034 --> 00:14:33,335
What's your class right now?

197
00:14:37,130 --> 00:14:40,065
See you at the dean's office.

198
00:14:42,045 --> 00:14:43,758
Deserve.

199
00:14:51,965 --> 00:14:54,211
(Loser.)

200
00:15:07,871 --> 00:15:09,372
What's with you, Florence?

201
00:15:09,372 --> 00:15:10,540
It's your first day of classes

202
00:15:10,540 --> 00:15:12,608
and you've been called
to the dean's office right away.

203
00:15:13,710 --> 00:15:15,178
You're really a failure.

204
00:15:15,178 --> 00:15:16,915
You'll even destroy a bench.

205
00:15:16,915 --> 00:15:19,749
What's with you, Florencia?

206
00:15:20,960 --> 00:15:23,353
You're such a failure.

207
00:15:23,353 --> 00:15:25,088
Are you okay?

208
00:15:25,088 --> 00:15:27,657
Don't let one bad day discourage you.

209
00:15:27,657 --> 00:15:30,894
Trust me, tomorrow will be much better.

210
00:15:30,894 --> 00:15:33,395
Hi, I'm Antonia.

211
00:15:35,402 --> 00:15:38,168
And if we stay in this relationship,

212
00:15:38,168 --> 00:15:45,207
the more I'd get hurt
and the more we'll hurt each other.

213
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:52,402
I agree.

214
00:15:52,402 --> 00:15:54,350
You're right.

215
00:15:54,350 --> 00:15:57,353
This will be better for both of us.

216
00:16:11,674 --> 00:16:13,957
Florence. Florence Dela Cruz at your service.

217
00:16:13,957 --> 00:16:17,640
And so that you won't forget,
give me an F, give me an L,

218
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,441
give me an...

219
00:16:21,023 --> 00:16:24,092
Just Florence.

220
00:16:25,033 --> 00:16:28,707
Wow, you really seem like a fun person.

221
00:16:28,707 --> 00:16:30,820
Is that why you're here in the dean's office?

222
00:16:30,820 --> 00:16:33,522
Did you have too much fun?

223
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:36,059
Huh?

224
00:16:36,059 --> 00:16:40,162
I'm sorry, I was just trying
to cheer you up...

225
00:16:40,162 --> 00:16:43,299
but it seems my sense of humor failed.

226
00:16:43,299 --> 00:16:44,437
No.

227
00:16:44,437 --> 00:16:48,100
Actually, the reason why I'm here is
that I had too much anger.

228
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:50,362
I lost my mind

229
00:16:50,362 --> 00:16:52,778
and did a lot of barking in the library
a while ago,

230
00:16:52,778 --> 00:16:57,441
that's why the librarian sent me here
for disciplinary action.

231
00:16:57,441 --> 00:17:00,383
Wow, you really weren't kidding.

232
00:17:00,383 --> 00:17:02,775
You must have been very upset

233
00:17:02,775 --> 00:17:05,754
to forget to keep quiet in the library.

234
00:17:06,788 --> 00:17:08,404
Well, that happens if you find out

235
00:17:08,404 --> 00:17:10,793
that the messages from the doves
are not for you.

236
00:17:10,793 --> 00:17:12,896
Excuse me?

237
00:17:12,896 --> 00:17:15,668
I mean, how about you? Why are you here?

238
00:17:15,668 --> 00:17:19,072
Well, I'm actually here
because I want to talk to the dean.

239
00:17:19,072 --> 00:17:21,471
Since last year I was the top student,

240
00:17:21,471 --> 00:17:25,198
I was highly recommended
by the fundamental chairs and faculty staff

241
00:17:25,198 --> 00:17:29,078
to be this year's
head of the university's student body.

242
00:17:29,078 --> 00:17:31,314
Wow, really?

243
00:17:31,314 --> 00:17:33,583
That's exciting.

244
00:17:33,583 --> 00:17:38,168
Well, it isn't something I look forward to,
to be honest.

245
00:17:38,168 --> 00:17:39,742
Aside from the heavy work,

246
00:17:39,742 --> 00:17:42,051
being the head of
the students here in Gyronella

247
00:17:42,051 --> 00:17:43,993
comes with tremendous pressure.

248
00:17:43,993 --> 00:17:46,596
Imagine, everyone who has gone
through this position

249
00:17:46,596 --> 00:17:49,625
ended up with very successful careers.

250
00:17:49,625 --> 00:17:53,002
Senators, supreme court justices,

251
00:17:53,002 --> 00:17:56,672
cabinet secretaries, CEOs.

252
00:17:59,541 --> 00:18:03,177
How about Ms. Universe?

253
00:18:08,051 --> 00:18:09,667
None yet.

254
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:18,109
But I can definitely be the first.

255
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:20,730
That made me nervous.

256
00:18:20,730 --> 00:18:22,516
I was just joking.

257
00:18:22,516 --> 00:18:24,100
I'm just making you laugh.

258
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,201
Thank you.

259
00:18:25,201 --> 00:18:27,303
No worries.

260
00:18:27,303 --> 00:18:31,507
Anyway, you're not the only one
having a bad day.

261
00:18:32,375 --> 00:18:35,907
You? Bad day?

262
00:18:37,047 --> 00:18:38,481
You're already having a bad day
with that beauty?

263
00:18:38,481 --> 00:18:40,383
What if it's a good day?

264
00:18:40,383 --> 00:18:42,651
You'll be more beautiful.

265
00:18:43,786 --> 00:18:45,822
Well, the difference is...

266
00:18:45,822 --> 00:18:50,826
I kind of expected that this day is coming.

267
00:18:53,514 --> 00:18:54,801
Huh?

268
00:19:02,405 --> 00:19:04,086
Why?

269
00:19:04,086 --> 00:19:06,775
What happened?

270
00:19:11,578 --> 00:19:15,102
Well, I... I have...

271
00:19:15,102 --> 00:19:18,220
I just ended things with my boyfriend.

272
00:19:28,164 --> 00:19:29,766
Are the kids home?

273
00:19:29,766 --> 00:19:35,338
They're in their rooms now.
Owen and Aldus, Tristan and Troy.

274
00:19:35,338 --> 00:19:39,208
I don't think they'll eat, Sir,
because they ate in school.

275
00:19:39,208 --> 00:19:43,049
Nero on the other hand
is still in the school library.

276
00:19:43,049 --> 00:19:46,676
He's finishing something,
according to Dencio.

277
00:19:46,676 --> 00:19:48,451
How about Florence?

278
00:19:48,451 --> 00:19:51,687
Oh well, she sent me a message.

279
00:19:51,687 --> 00:19:55,775
She said, she was just fixing something.

280
00:19:55,775 --> 00:19:57,969
I pity Florence.

281
00:19:57,969 --> 00:20:01,197
She needs to wake up early to cook for us.

282
00:20:01,197 --> 00:20:03,699
And now with the added pressure of school,

283
00:20:03,699 --> 00:20:07,806
maybe she might not be able to
handle the pressures of life.

284
00:20:07,806 --> 00:20:12,125
Trust me, Don Ferell,
Florence doesn't feel that way.

285
00:20:12,125 --> 00:20:16,946
Maybe she's energized
because of her opportunities now.

286
00:20:16,946 --> 00:20:20,922
Truthfully, a heart with big dreams

287
00:20:20,922 --> 00:20:25,555
doesn't easily get pressured or get tired.

288
00:20:25,555 --> 00:20:31,761
Yes, but let's help her
to achieve her dreams...

289
00:20:31,761 --> 00:20:36,265
since our agreement is
she'll cook for the kids.

290
00:20:36,265 --> 00:20:38,734
Now that they're back to school,

291
00:20:38,734 --> 00:20:41,303
she doesn't have to wake up early.

292
00:20:42,338 --> 00:20:46,109
But how about you, Don Ferell?
You like her home cooking so much.

293
00:20:46,109 --> 00:20:47,359
True.

294
00:20:47,359 --> 00:20:50,847
I guess I'll just have to
settle with your cooking.

295
00:20:50,847 --> 00:20:55,318
Don Ferell, don't belittle my cooking skills.

296
00:20:55,318 --> 00:21:00,789
After all, I wouldn't have won Dencio's heart
if not for my cooking.

297
00:21:01,794 --> 00:21:05,037
Well, try to win my heart with your cooking.

298
00:21:05,037 --> 00:21:06,130
Let's see.

299
00:21:06,130 --> 00:21:08,498
Challenge accepted, Sir.

300
00:21:08,498 --> 00:21:10,432
Anytime.

301
00:21:15,071 --> 00:21:17,240
See, I told you.

302
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:18,959
The dean is easy to talk to.

303
00:21:18,959 --> 00:21:22,345
Thank you for backing me up
with the dean earlier.

304
00:21:22,345 --> 00:21:23,746
Don't mention it.

305
00:21:23,746 --> 00:21:28,851
You know, being noisy in the library
is actually a minor offense.

306
00:21:28,851 --> 00:21:31,454
Just don't do it again.

307
00:21:31,454 --> 00:21:33,389
It was really nice meeting you, by the way.

308
00:21:33,389 --> 00:21:36,392
Nice meeting you too, Antonia.

309
00:21:36,392 --> 00:21:38,828
Anyway, it's getting late.

310
00:21:38,828 --> 00:21:39,962
Do you have a ride?

311
00:21:39,962 --> 00:21:42,999
Yes, maybe it's waiting for me
around the corner.

312
00:21:42,999 --> 00:21:45,841
Okay, I'll go ahead.

313
00:21:45,841 --> 00:21:47,236
I'll see you around.

314
00:21:47,236 --> 00:21:51,006
Thanks again for what you did earlier.
I'll see you around Antonia.

315
00:22:02,418 --> 00:22:05,561
I'll go here. There's a way here.

316
00:22:15,431 --> 00:22:17,967
You're the target enemy #1 of Aylip.

317
00:22:17,967 --> 00:22:19,769
And they have a lot of members here in school

318
00:22:19,769 --> 00:22:22,571
so you have a big problem.

319
00:22:30,613 --> 00:22:32,081
Why are you following me?

320
00:22:32,081 --> 00:22:33,182
Show yourself.

321
00:22:33,182 --> 00:22:34,550
Do you think I'm scared of you?

322
00:22:34,550 --> 00:22:36,251
Who are you?

323
00:22:38,154 --> 00:22:39,655
Why are you following me?

324
00:22:39,655 --> 00:22:42,992
I came from the library when I saw you.

325
00:22:42,992 --> 00:22:44,360
What do you need?

326
00:22:44,360 --> 00:22:46,562
I already called Mr. Dencio.

327
00:22:46,562 --> 00:22:48,464
Just ride home with us.

328
00:22:48,464 --> 00:22:49,832
I'll take the trike home.

329
00:22:49,832 --> 00:22:51,500
There are no more tricycles.

330
00:22:51,500 --> 00:22:53,769
I'm sure there are a lot of tricycles
on the highway.

331
00:22:53,769 --> 00:22:55,704
I'll wait there.

332
00:22:56,505 --> 00:22:58,741
Don't you want to take just one vehicle?

333
00:22:58,741 --> 00:23:01,143
That's less pollution.

334
00:23:01,143 --> 00:23:03,249
Do you know what's less pollution?

335
00:23:03,249 --> 00:23:07,086
That's to walk home,
the best way to defeat global warming,

336
00:23:07,086 --> 00:23:09,385
zero carbon emissions.

337
00:23:09,385 --> 00:23:10,686
Are you sure?

338
00:23:10,686 --> 00:23:12,351
It's dark there.

339
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:20,462
Okay, I'll go with you.

340
00:23:34,710 --> 00:23:36,145
Where's Nero?

341
00:23:36,145 --> 00:23:37,780
Here, I'm texting him.

342
00:23:37,780 --> 00:23:39,039
Where is he?

343
00:23:39,039 --> 00:23:41,017
Don't tell me
it's just the first day of school

344
00:23:41,017 --> 00:23:43,953
and he acted like a good student.

345
00:23:43,953 --> 00:23:46,822
Nero is Grandpa's standard
when it comes to school.

346
00:23:46,822 --> 00:23:49,025
That's why we're pressured.

347
00:23:49,025 --> 00:23:51,703
He said he's on his way home.

348
00:23:51,703 --> 00:23:53,905
And Florence is with him.

349
00:23:54,930 --> 00:23:57,024
They're together?

350
00:23:57,024 --> 00:23:58,539
After the incident,

351
00:23:58,539 --> 00:24:02,405
the dean talked to her,
that's why she stayed in school till late.

352
00:24:02,405 --> 00:24:04,974
Good thing they saw each other.

353
00:24:04,974 --> 00:24:07,042
Why, Bro, is there a problem?

354
00:24:14,091 --> 00:24:15,926
What's his problem?

355
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:18,954
I don't know.

356
00:24:18,954 --> 00:24:21,757
To be honest, I don't want to ask.

357
00:24:21,757 --> 00:24:24,927
Just like a story, the plot thickens.

358
00:24:24,927 --> 00:24:27,630
Maybe it's his first day.

359
00:24:27,630 --> 00:24:29,531
Heavy flow.

360
00:24:34,437 --> 00:24:38,074
So, Nero, how's your first day of school?

361
00:24:38,074 --> 00:24:39,750
Are you okay?

362
00:24:39,750 --> 00:24:40,977
I'm just okay.

363
00:24:40,977 --> 00:24:42,578
How about you?

364
00:24:42,578 --> 00:24:44,446
I'm okay too.

365
00:24:48,448 --> 00:24:51,036
How come you don't look convinced?

366
00:24:51,036 --> 00:24:53,122
From what I heard,

367
00:24:53,122 --> 00:24:56,025
it looks like you had a bad day at school.

368
00:24:56,025 --> 00:24:57,931
So what?

369
00:24:57,931 --> 00:25:02,064
What? Will you lecture me too?

370
00:25:02,064 --> 00:25:06,142
What's with the Ferells?
Do you guys really want to protect me?

371
00:25:06,142 --> 00:25:08,260
What's this, Messianic complex,

372
00:25:08,260 --> 00:25:12,341
or all of you can't help
but be a Prince Charming?

373
00:25:12,341 --> 00:25:15,144
Do you all want to save a damsel in distress?

374
00:25:15,144 --> 00:25:18,346
And with my situation,
I am a damsel in distress.

375
00:25:18,346 --> 00:25:20,648
You know, Nero, for your information,

376
00:25:20,648 --> 00:25:22,850
I am not your damsel in distress.

377
00:25:22,850 --> 00:25:24,653
I am my own woman.

378
00:25:24,653 --> 00:25:27,288
I don't need men to save me

379
00:25:27,288 --> 00:25:33,160
because whatever fate throws at me,
I can face that by myself.

380
00:25:39,600 --> 00:25:42,437
It's not bad to ask for help from others,

381
00:25:42,437 --> 00:25:46,173
and it's not good
that you always keep everything to yourself.

382
00:25:49,355 --> 00:25:52,380
Don't talk as if you're not hurting

383
00:25:52,380 --> 00:25:54,982
or act like you're not having a hard time.

384
00:25:54,982 --> 00:25:57,452
Because no matter how you hide
what you're feeling,

385
00:25:57,452 --> 00:26:01,189
I'm sure sometimes your heart
is asking for an ally.

386
00:26:01,189 --> 00:26:03,791
It's not a weakness to ask for help.

387
00:26:03,791 --> 00:26:05,793
Sometimes, that's the way things are.

388
00:26:05,793 --> 00:26:08,796
We need others so we can bounce back.

389
00:26:08,796 --> 00:26:12,734
Sometimes, be true to what you're feeling.

390
00:26:12,734 --> 00:26:15,536
Don't be scared to show it to others.

391
00:26:19,352 --> 00:26:20,879
Wow!

392
00:26:21,567 --> 00:26:22,863
Wow.

393
00:26:24,371 --> 00:26:26,013
Be true?

394
00:26:26,013 --> 00:26:27,926
Really?

395
00:26:47,969 --> 00:26:50,938
<i>It's not bad to ask for help from others,</i>

396
00:26:50,938 --> 00:26:53,941
